 Per-key operations are linearized while unrelated keys may progress concurrently. Process spawn, external I/O, fsync and provider waits are slow paths and must not execute under a global registry lock. At capacity, admission is rejected before starting a process or publishing an accepted effect.
 
+
+### Startup observation and global-lock scope
+
+`JobManager::start` copies an existing `RunningJob` owner in a separate statement
+before it waits on `StartupGate` or consults the registry/journal. A temporary
+running-map guard in a successful `if let` arm would otherwise survive across
+those operations, including in Rust edition 2024. The global map protects only
+lookup/publication/removal; per-start-shard and per-job lifecycle ordering remain
+unchanged. This change does not increase capacity or make a shard lock timed.
+
+Each startup observation wait has one monotonic 30-second budget. Condition
+variable notifications recheck the actual state and use the remaining budget;
+repeated or spurious notifications cannot renew it. A still-pending gate returns
+`JobRuntimeError::Control` with an explicit uncertain-startup diagnostic. The
+waiter does not change the gate, release the job's admission permit, append a
+terminal, signal a process, cancel a start or authorize a retry. A later genuine
+Ready, Failed or Terminal transition retains its existing meaning. For effectful
+controls this wait precedes `begin_control`, so expiry admits no control effect.
+
+This is a bound on condition-variable waiting, not a hard real-time bound on the
+whole API. Mutex ownership, start-shard/lifecycle locks, filesystem operations and
+OS scheduling are not preempted by this change. Installed cancellation latency,
+contention and recovery remain L2/L5 qualification requirements.
+
+The manager's permanent tests cover global-map availability while a duplicate
+waits, finite pending waits, repeated notifications, and real failure/terminal
+transitions after an observer expires. The map regression uses a real local
+stdin-blocked child and an observed owner reference, releases its barriers and
+cleans up the child before asserting, including on the defective base.
+
